{
  "title": "Pleomorphic Sarcoma of Bone (Malignant Fibrous Histiocytoma)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8030/pleomorphic-sarcoma-of-bone-malignant-fibrous-histiocytoma",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Feb 17 2022",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pleomorphic Sarcoma of Bone, formerly known as Malignant Fibrous Histiocytoma, are rare malignant histiocytic lesions of bone most commonly found in the metaphysis of long bones. Patients typically present between the ages of 20 to 80 with painful, regional masses.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with biopsy showing pleomorphic spindle cells and histiocytic cells in storiform pattern.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually neo-adjuvant chemotherapy, limb salvage surgical resection, followed by adjuvant chemotherapy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "comprises < 2% of all primary malignant bone tumors",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "second most common bone sarcoma in adults after chondrosarcoma",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "affects individuals 20 to 80 years of age",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "highest rates of affected patients in 2nd to 4th decades",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "male > female (3:2)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "more common in Caucasians than African Americans or Asians",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "75% of cases from appendicular skeleton",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "often **metaphysis** of long bones",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "primarily distal femur, proximal tibia, proximal humerus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**25% arise as secondary lesion from bone infarct, Paget disease, or prior radiation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mutations of the tumor suppressor gene p53 have been implicated in tumorgenesis of secondary MFH of bone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**new, painful** mass",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "can present with **pathologic fracture**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
